{"repositoryId":236570305,"availability":"available","full":"pubkey/event-reduce","name":"event-reduce","description":"An algorithm to optimize database queries that run multiple times https://pubkey.github.io/event-reduce/","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":754,"forks":24,"created":"2020-01-27T19:07:28Z","updated":"2026-10-17T04:28:22Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://pubkey.github.io/event-reduce","topics":["bdd","database","event-reduce","live-queries","nosql-database","observability","oplog-tailing","realtime","realtime-database","realtime-queries"],"demo":"https://pubkey.github.io/event-reduce/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:42.329Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:42.329Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:42.329Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T22:45:42.329Z","stars":754,"forks":24}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Update live query results from change events without re-running the query","Live demo · JavaScript implementation · How it works · FAQ","EventReduce is an algorithm for live queries (also called reactive or realtime queries). When a document is inserted, updated or deleted, it takes the old query results and the change event and computes the new results in memory, without querying the database again. It works like a lightweight form of incremental view maintenance for a single query over a single table or collection."],"features":["94% of write events in the browser demo are handled without re-running the query","Up to 12× faster delivery of new query results after a write","Works with any database that gives you a change stream: MongoDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL, IndexedDB, SQLite, in-memory stores...","Proven in production as the query engine behind the live queries of RxDB"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pubkey/event-reduce/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"bee36613c92b288537d6a78bf261fac5df73d256452195fb4ce73f9ab53247